-- Employment Claims Act 2016 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: PART 3, EMPLOYMENT CLAIMS, Division 4 and section 27 (ss 23 to 27).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.  Target compiler: main (build 109).
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is a yes the Act gives; JUST FALSE is a no the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").

§ `Part 3 -- Division 4, Appeals`

§§ `s 23 -- appeal to the General Division of the High Court`

-- s 23(2): an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court only if permission to appeal is given by a District Court.
-- src:1594 | (2) An appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court under
-- src:1595 | this section only if permission to appeal is given by a District Court.
@ref s 23(2) (src:1594-1595)
GIVEN `a District Court has given permission to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) the condition that a District Court gives permission to appeal is met` MEANS
    IF `a District Court has given permission to appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court under this section only if permission to appeal is given by a District Court"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 23(1): any party to proceedings before a tribunal may appeal against an order under section 22(1) (a) on any ground involving a question of law, or (b) on the ground that the claim was outside the tribunal's jurisdiction.
-- src:1583 | 23.—(1) Any party to proceedings before a tribunal may appeal to
-- src:1584 | the General Division of the High Court against an order made by the
-- src:1585 | tribunal under section 22(1) —
-- src:1587 | (a) on any ground involving a question of law; or
-- src:1589 | (b) on the ground that the claim was outside the jurisdiction of
-- src:1590 | the tribunal.
@ref s 23(1) (src:1583-1590)
GIVEN `the person is a party to the proceedings before the tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was made by the tribunal under section 22(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `Ground of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) the party may appeal to the General Division of the High Court against the order on the ground` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party to the proceedings before the tribunal` AND `the order was made by the tribunal under section 22(1)` AND (ground EQUALS `A ground involving a question of law` OR ground EQUALS `That the claim was outside the jurisdiction of the tribunal`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [open question; reviewer expected JUST FALSE]: the right is for "any party", against "an order made by the tribunal under section 22(1)", on the two grounds named; section 25(2)(a) bars the High Court from reversing a finding of fact, but this section does not say in so many words that an appeal on a question of fact cannot be brought
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 23(1): the appeal is to the General Division of the High Court.
-- src:1583 | 23.—(1) Any party to proceedings before a tribunal may appeal to
-- src:1584 | the General Division of the High Court against an order made by the
-- src:1585 | tribunal under section 22(1) —
@ref s 23(1) (src:1583-1585)
GIVEN court IS A `Court named in the Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) the court is the one to which the party may appeal` MEANS
    IF court EQUALS `The General Division of the High Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the appeal is "to the General Division of the High Court"; the clause names the court and carries no "only"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 23(1) and (2) together: may the party appeal?
-- src:1583 | 23.—(1) Any party to proceedings before a tribunal may appeal to
-- src:1584 | the General Division of the High Court against an order made by the
-- src:1585 | tribunal under section 22(1) —
-- src:1587 | (a) on any ground involving a question of law; or
-- src:1589 | (b) on the ground that the claim was outside the jurisdiction of
-- src:1590 | the tribunal.
-- src:1594 | (2) An appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court under
-- src:1595 | this section only if permission to appeal is given by a District Court.
@ref s 23(1) and (2) (src:1583-1595)
GIVEN `section 23(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `section 23(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) and (2) an appeal lies to the General Division of the High Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if permission to appeal is given by a District Court" (permission has not been given)
        IF `section 23(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `section 23(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `section 23(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [open question; reviewer expected JUST FALSE]: the right to appeal in (1) is limited to the two grounds; and, where permission is not shown, the condition in (2) is not yet shown to be met
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 23(3): where the only reason for appealing is to rectify anything in section 22(10)(a) to (d), a District Court may, instead of giving permission to appeal, (a) extend the time under section 22(10) for the correction of the order and (b) remit the matter to a tribunal for the correction.
