-- s 23(4): each of three kinds of District Court order is final and not subject to any appeal.
-- src:1616 | (4) Each of the following is final and is not subject to any appeal:
-- src:1618 | (a) any order of a District Court giving or refusing permission
-- src:1619 | under subsection (2);
-- src:1623 | (b) any order of a District Court extending or refusing to
-- src:1624 | extend under subsection (3)(a) the time under
-- src:1625 | section 22(10) for the correction of an order made by a
-- src:1626 | tribunal;
-- src:1628 | (c) any order of a District Court remitting or refusing to remit
-- src:1629 | under subsection (3)(b) a matter to a tribunal.
@ref s 23(4) (src:1616-1629)
GIVEN order IS AN `Order of a District Court on an appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(4) the order is final and is not subject to any appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `An order giving or refusing permission under section 23(2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `An order extending or refusing to extend under section 23(3)(a) the time under section 22(10)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `An order remitting or refusing to remit under section 23(3)(b) a matter to a tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Each of the following is final" lists three orders and does not say that no other order is appealable
    WHEN `Another order` THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 24 -- stay of execution or enforcement`

-- s 24(1): an appeal does not operate as a stay of execution or enforcement unless a District Court or the General Division of the High Court orders otherwise.
-- src:1636 | 24.—(1) An appeal against an order made by a tribunal under
-- src:1637 | section 22(1) does not operate as a stay of execution or enforcement
-- src:1638 | of that order, unless a District Court or the General Division of the
-- src:1639 | High Court orders otherwise.
@ref s 24(1) (src:1636-1639)
GIVEN `a District Court or the General Division of the High Court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(1) the appeal by itself operates as a stay of execution or enforcement of the order` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a District Court or the General Division of the High Court orders otherwise`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal against an order made by a tribunal under section 22(1) does not operate as a stay of execution or enforcement of that order"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "unless a District Court or the General Division of the High Court orders otherwise" lifts the no; when a court does, the stay is by its order and the text does not say that the appeal itself operates as one (the twin below asks whether execution is stayed)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 24(1), the other half: an appeal does not operate as a stay unless a District Court or the General Division of the High Court orders otherwise, so execution is stayed pending an appeal where a court orders a stay.
-- src:1636 | 24.—(1) An appeal against an order made by a tribunal under
-- src:1637 | section 22(1) does not operate as a stay of execution or enforcement
-- src:1638 | of that order, unless a District Court or the General Division of the
-- src:1639 | High Court orders otherwise.
@ref s 24(1) (src:1636-1639)
GIVEN `an appeal has been brought against an order made by a tribunal under section 22(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a District Court or the General Division of the High Court orders a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(1) execution or enforcement of the order is stayed pending the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the rule is for "an appeal against an order made by a tribunal under section 22(1)"; where there is no appeal the clause is not spoken to
        IF (NOT `an appeal has been brought against an order made by a tribunal under section 22(1)`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `a District Court or the General Division of the High Court orders a stay` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal against an order made by a tribunal under section 22(1) does not operate as a stay of execution or enforcement of that order" (no court has ordered a stay)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 24(2): a District Court or the General Division of the High Court may direct that a stay be subject to any conditions it thinks fit, including as to costs, payment into court or security.
-- src:1645 | (2) A District Court or the General Division of the High Court may
-- src:1646 | direct that a stay of execution or enforcement (of an order made by a
-- src:1647 | tribunal) be subject to any conditions that the District Court or the
-- src:1648 | General Division of the High Court thinks fit to impose, including
-- src:1649 | conditions as to costs, payment into a District Court or the General
-- src:1650 | Division of the High Court, or the giving of security.
@ref s 24(2) (src:1645-1650)
GIVEN court IS A `Court named in the Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(2) the court may direct that a stay be subject to any conditions it thinks fit` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `The General Division of the High Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `A District Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the power is given to "a District Court or the General Division of the High Court"; the clause names who holds it and carries no "only"
    WHEN `A Magistrate's Court` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the same: another court is not named in the section
    WHEN `Another court` THEN NOTHING

-- s 24(3): any order or direction of a District Court on an application for a stay is final and not subject to any appeal.
-- src:1656 | (3) Any order or direction of a District Court on an application for a
-- src:1657 | stay of execution or enforcement (of an order made by a tribunal) is
-- src:1658 | final and is not subject to any appeal.
@ref s 24(3) (src:1656-1658)
GIVEN `the order or direction is a District Court's, on an application for a stay of execution or enforcement of an order made by a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(3) the order or direction is final and is not subject to any appeal` MEANS
    IF `the order or direction is a District Court's, on an application for a stay of execution or enforcement of an order made by a tribunal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: "Any order or direction of a District Court on an application for a stay"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 24(4): the General Division of the High Court may order a stay or give a direction under (2) only if (a) a District Court has given permission to appeal under section 23(2) and (b) no application was made to any District Court for a stay.
-- src:1662 | (4) The General Division of the High Court may order a stay of
-- src:1663 | execution or enforcement of an order made by a tribunal, or give a
-- src:1664 | direction under subsection (2), only if —
-- src:1666 | (a) a District Court has given under section 23(2) permission
-- src:1667 | to appeal against the order made by the tribunal; and
-- src:1671 | (b) no application was made to any District Court for a stay of
-- src:1672 | execution or enforcement of the order made by the
-- src:1673 | tribunal.
@ref s 24(4) (src:1662-1673)
GIVEN `a District Court has given under section 23(2) permission to appeal against the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application was made to any District Court for a stay of execution or enforcement of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(4) the conditions for the General Division of the High Court to order a stay are met` MEANS
    IF `a District Court has given under section 23(2) permission to appeal against the order` AND (NOT `an application was made to any District Court for a stay of execution or enforcement of the order`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may order a stay ..., or give a direction under subsection (2), only if — (a) a District Court has given ... permission to appeal ...; and (b) no application was made to any District Court for a stay" (one of them is not so)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 25 -- powers of the High Court on appeal`

-- s 25(1) and (2): what the General Division of the High Court may do on an appeal.
-- src:1680 | 25.—(1) On an appeal against an order made by a tribunal, the
-- src:1682 | General Division of the High Court may —
-- src:1683 | (a) dismiss the appeal;
-- src:1684 | (b) allow the appeal and set aside or vary the order; or
-- src:1689 | (c) remit the matter to the tribunal for reconsideration, or order
-- src:1690 | a rehearing of the matter by a different tribunal, with any
-- src:1691 | directions that the General Division of the High Court
-- src:1692 | thinks fit to give.
-- src:1696 | (2) The General Division of the High Court may also make on the
-- src:1697 | appeal any other orders (including an order as to costs and expenses)
-- src:1698 | that the General Division of the High Court thinks fit, but must not —
-- src:1700 | (a) reverse or vary any determination made by a tribunal on a
-- src:1701 | question of fact; or
-- src:1703 | (b) receive further evidence.
@ref s 25(1) and (2) (src:1680-1703)
GIVEN step IS A `Step on appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25 the General Division of the High Court may take the step on the appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER step
    WHEN `Dismiss the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Allow the appeal and set aside or vary the order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Remit the matter to the tribunal for reconsideration, or order a rehearing by a different tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Make any other order, including an order as to costs and expenses` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but must not — (a) reverse or vary any determination made by a tribunal on a question of fact"
    WHEN `Reverse or vary a determination made by a tribunal on a question of fact` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but must not — ... (b) receive further evidence"
    WHEN `Receive further evidence` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): section 25(1) lists three things and (2) adds "any other orders"; a step that is neither is not spoken to
    WHEN `Some other step` THEN NOTHING

