§§ `s 26 -- finality of the High Court's decision`

-- s 26: any judgment, order or direction of the General Division of the High Court on an appeal against a tribunal's order, or on an application for a stay of its execution or enforcement, is final.
-- src:1730 | 26. Any judgment, order or direction of the General Division of the
-- src:1731 | High Court on any of the following matters is final:
-- src:1733 | (a) an appeal against an order made by a tribunal;
-- src:1735 | (b) an application for a stay of execution or enforcement of an
-- src:1736 | order made by a tribunal.
@ref s 26 (src:1730-1736)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter decided by the General Division of the High Court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 the judgment, order or direction of the General Division of the High Court is final` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `An appeal against an order made by a tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `An application for a stay of execution or enforcement of an order made by a tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the section makes final the decisions "on any of the following matters" and says nothing of other matters
    WHEN `Another matter` THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 27 -- burden of proof`

-- s 27(1): in proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court, a person who alleges that the person is not the employer or employee of the claimant, or is not a person with a duty under one of three Acts, bears the burden of proving it.
-- src:1746 | 27.—(1) In any proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the
-- src:1747 | General Division of the High Court, a person who makes any of the
-- src:1748 | following allegations bears the burden of proving that allegation:
-- src:1750 | (a) an allegation that the person is not the employer or
-- src:1751 | employee of the claimant;
-- src:1753 | (b) an allegation that the person is not a person who has a duty
-- src:1754 | under any of the following Acts to do or abstain from doing
-- src:1755 | any thing:
-- src:1757 | (i) the Child Development Co‑Savings Act 2001;
-- src:1759 | (ii) the Employment Act 1968;
-- src:1761 | (iii) the Retirement and Re‑employment Act 1993.
@ref s 27(1) (src:1746-1761)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      allegation IS AN `Allegation about a duty or a relationship`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) the person who makes the allegation bears the burden of proving it` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court` AND (allegation EQUALS `That the person is not the employer or employee of the claimant` OR allegation EQUALS `That the person is not a person who has a duty under the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001, the Employment Act 1968 or the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the burden is placed for "any of the following allegations" in proceedings "under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court"; any other allegation is not spoken to
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 27(2)(a): where an employee is dismissed without notice under section 14(1) of the Employment Act 1968 and lodges a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of that Act, the employer bears the burden of proving the employee was dismissed with just cause or excuse.
