    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: "In any proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court, the following apply"; other proceedings are not spoken to
        IF (NOT `the proceedings are under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the employee is dismissed without notice by an employer under section 14(1) of the Employment Act 1968` AND `the employee lodges a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of that Act against the employer` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an employee is dismissed without notice ... and the employee lodges a claim mentioned in section 14(2)" [ruled (b)] (the employee was not dismissed without notice, or lodged no such claim)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

