@ref s 27(2)(b) (src:1765-1780)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is dismissed with notice by an employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of dismissal is or purports to be given on the ground that there has been poor performance or misconduct by the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2)(b) the employer bears the burden of proving the ground for giving the notice of dismissal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: "In any proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court, the following apply"; other proceedings are not spoken to
        IF (NOT `the proceedings are under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the employee is dismissed with notice by an employer` AND `the notice of dismissal is or purports to be given on the ground that there has been poor performance or misconduct by the employee` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an employee is dismissed with notice ... and the notice of dismissal is or purports to be given on the ground that there has been poor performance or misconduct" [ruled (b)] (the employee was not dismissed with notice, or the notice was given on another ground)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 27(2)(c): where a notice of dismissal is given to a female employee in the circumstances in section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c) of the Employment Act 1968 and she lodges a claim mentioned in section 84(2), the employer bears the burden of proving she was dismissed with sufficient cause.
