-- src:1785 | and the female employee lodges a claim mentioned in
-- src:1786 | section 84(2) of that Act against the employer — the
-- src:1787 | employer bears the burden of proving the allegation that
-- src:1788 | the female employee was dismissed with sufficient cause;
@ref s 27(2)(c) (src:1765-1788)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice of dismissal is given to a female employee by an employer in the circumstances mentioned in section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c) of the Employment Act 1968` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the female employee lodges a claim mentioned in section 84(2) of that Act against the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2)(c) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee was dismissed with sufficient cause` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: "In any proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court, the following apply"; other proceedings are not spoken to
        IF (NOT `the proceedings are under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `a notice of dismissal is given to a female employee by an employer in the circumstances mentioned in section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c) of the Employment Act 1968` AND `the female employee lodges a claim mentioned in section 84(2) of that Act against the employer` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a notice of dismissal is given to a female employee ... in the circumstances mentioned in section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c)" [ruled (b)] (the notice was not so given, or she lodged no such claim)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

