@ref s 27(2)(d) (src:1765-1803)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice of dismissal is given to a female employee mentioned in section 12(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 by an employer in the circumstances mentioned in section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c) of the Employment Act 1968, as applied to her` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the female employee lodges a claim mentioned in section 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968, as applied to her, against the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(2)(d) the employer bears the burden of proving that the female employee mentioned in section 12(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 was dismissed with sufficient cause` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: "In any proceedings under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court, the following apply"; other proceedings are not spoken to
        IF (NOT `the proceedings are under this Act before a tribunal or the General Division of the High Court`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `a notice of dismissal is given to a female employee mentioned in section 12(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 by an employer in the circumstances mentioned in section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c) of the Employment Act 1968, as applied to her` AND `the female employee lodges a claim mentioned in section 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968, as applied to her, against the employer` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a notice of dismissal is given to a female employee mentioned in section 12(1) of the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 ... in the circumstances mentioned in section 84(1)(a), (b) or (c)" [ruled (b)] (the notice was not so given, or she lodged no such claim)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
